  "description": "Faithfully extracted from KernelGenBench cuBLAS test_cublasZgemvStridedBatched.py. Complex128 strided-batched GEMV over real 3D/2D tensors via the real cuBLAS baseline. _random_tensor does not support complex, so A/x/y are built by gen_inputs as (randn(float64)+1j*randn(float64)).to(complex128). trans is passed as int (0='N',1='T') exactly as the test converts before calling the baseline. lda=M, strideA=M*N; for trans=0 lenx=N,leny=M; for trans=1 lenx=M,leny=N; stridex=lenx, stridey=leny, incx=incy=1. alpha/beta: only the real-valued (imag=0) combos from the test are used, since JSON scalars cannot encode complex; the op's complex-scalar path is still exercised via complex A/x/y (baseline casts alpha/beta to complex128). reference mutates y in place and returns it. Requires kernelgenbench + cuBLAS at eval time.",
